# Cerebellum environment. Copy to cere.env next to service_ctl.sh, chmod 0600,
# and fill in the blanks. It holds a bearer token and a cloud API key: never
# commit it, never print it into a transcript.
#
# Every key in the Listener, Voice presence, Upstream and Mouth sections is
# REQUIRED and none has a default. Exceptions: the TLS pair is optional as a
# pair; DASHSCOPE_API_KEY may equally come from the duoduo dotenv file or the
# workspace config; CEREBELLUM_ASR_PROMPT_HINT must be present but may be empty,
# and CEREBELLUM_ASR_PROMPT_BASE is required only when the hint is not empty. That is deliberate. These values decide barge-in latency, which model answers, and
# whether room audio leaves the machine encrypted; a plausible-looking constant
# invented by the code would ferment into "the value" without anyone deciding it.
# A missing key is a hard refusal at boot, naming what to set.

# ── Listener ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Bind address. Wildcards (0.0.0.0, ::, *, empty) are REFUSED: this socket
# carries continuous room audio, and a deployment machine usually has a public
# interface. Name the private-network address the channel reaches, or 127.0.0.1
# when the channel runs on this same machine.
CEREBELLUM_HOST=
CEREBELLUM_PORT=30077
# Bearer token the channel must present. Required on a private network too.
# User-provided: generate a long random string, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`.
CEREBELLUM_TOKEN=
# WebSocket heartbeat period in ms. A half-open TCP connection is otherwise
# undetectable. 15000 matches the channel's own heartbeat_ms; the two are one
# convention declared twice, so change them together.
CEREBELLUM_HEARTBEAT_MS=15000

# TLS certificate and private key PATHS. Optional AS A PAIR: both present means
# wss://, both absent means plaintext ws:// for loopback debugging only, and
# exactly one present is refused at boot. The channel rejects any non-wss URL
# that is not loopback, so on a real deployment these are effectively required.
# User-provided; see README.md for minting them.
CEREBELLUM_TLS_CERT=
CEREBELLUM_TLS_KEY=

# ── Voice presence (Silero) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Path to the Silero artifact shipped at packages/cerebellum/artifacts/silero-vad.onnx.
# Its SHA-256 is verified on every load and a mismatch is fatal: nothing is
# downloaded at runtime. Absent means this machine has no voice detector, and
# there is nothing to fall back to - the energy detector was deleted, not
# disabled.
CEREBELLUM_SILERO_MODEL=/opt/ambient/cerebellum/packages/cerebellum/artifacts/silero-vad.onnx
# The three numbers below are ONE operating point, and it is PROVISIONAL: these
# are the upstream vendor's shipped values, adopted as a starting point. They are
# not a tuned calibration and no labelled curve has been measured against this
# room type. Treat a change as an experiment with a result, not as a tweak.
#
# Speech probability at or above which a hop opens a voice candidate.
CEREBELLUM_VOICE_THRESHOLD=0.5
# Hysteresis below the onset threshold: a hop counts as silence under
# (threshold - offset).
CEREBELLUM_VOICE_NEG_THRESHOLD_OFFSET=0.15
# A candidate shorter than this many ms is rejected before it reaches the ear.
# This is the knob that trades futile transcription calls against missed short
# backchannels.
CEREBELLUM_VOICE_MIN_SPEECH_MS=250
#
# Not one of the three vendor values above.
# A closed segment reaches the ear only if it holds a run of consecutive hops at
# or above the threshold longer than this many ms (measured on the segment alone).
# A shorter run lets more faint, broken audio reach the ear, which writes text
# nobody said; a longer one starts dropping short real words. 192 was chosen on
# recorded room audio, where it blocked transcripts invented on near-silent
# segments without dropping real speech. Re-check it on your own rooms.
CEREBELLUM_VOICE_MIN_RUN_MS=192

# ── Upstream services, models and state ─────────────────────────────────────
# Transcription + diarization, the FULL route. One call returns both the text and
# the speaker split, and there is no degraded path: a fallback that returned text
# without attribution would silently drop half of what the caller asked for.
AMBIENT_MOSS_URL=http://127.0.0.1:30180/v1/audio/transcriptions
# Transcription prompt. The server REPLACES its default instruction with a
# non-empty `prompt`, so a hint is sent as BASE followed by HINT. BASE must equal
# the server's default instruction byte for byte: DEFAULT_MOSS_TRANSCRIBE_DIARIZE_PROMPT
# in vllm/model_executor/models/moss_transcribe_diarize.py, the same text as the
# MOSS-Transcribe-Diarize README's default prompt. No endpoint exposes it, so
# re-check it when the server's vLLM is upgraded. HINT must be declared; empty
# sends no prompt (the server's default). Both are sent untrimmed; keep the
# single quotes, this file is sourced by bash.
# Rationale: for Mandarin rooms. With this hint the ear writes Chinese or
# nothing for faint speech instead of invented English, and keeps English terms.
CEREBELLUM_ASR_PROMPT_BASE='请将音频转写为文本，每一段需以起始时间戳和说话人编号（[S01]、[S02]、[S03]…）开头，正文为对应的语音内容，并在段末标注结束时间戳，以清晰标明该段语音范围。'
CEREBELLUM_ASR_PROMPT_HINT='语音以普通话为主，其中的英文单词保留英文拼写；听不清的背景人声不要转写。'
# Streaming diarizer, the FULL WebSocket route. Follows each voice across a
# connection's audio; rows are numbered through its tracks. Unreachable means
# every row stays `V?` and transcripts flow as usual.
AMBIENT_DIARIZER_URL=ws://127.0.0.1:30182/v1/diarize/stream
# Voiceprint embedding, the FULL /embed URL. /healthz is resolved against its
# origin and its `model` field names the stored voiceprint space.
AMBIENT_SPEAKER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:30076/embed
# Labelling one utterance from its own audio while its diarizer track is not
# bound yet (a track binds after about 30 s of clean speech). A single-voice
# utterance at least MIN_S seconds long, outside our own playback, takes the
# best room voice by best-sample cosine when that score reaches FLOOR and leads
# the runner-up by at least MARGIN (a library of one voice has no runner-up, and
# FLOOR alone decides); otherwise it stays V?. The embedding starts when the
# segment closes and is never waited for: if it is still running when the rows
# are made they stay V?, and its result labels the track's later utterances.
# Later utterances of the same track carry the label until the track binds,
# which confirms or replaces it. These labels are never written into the voice
# library.
# Rationale (MIN_S, MARGIN): the two values trade labelled rows against wrong
# labels. A shorter MIN_S or a smaller MARGIN labels more utterances and
# mislabels more of them, and short utterances are the least reliable. 2 s and
# 0.05 were chosen on recorded room audio, with each utterance's own stream left
# out of the library as for a track that has not bound.
# Rationale (FLOOR): a person missing from the library still has a nearest
# voice, and the margin alone can give them its label. Their best scores sit
# well below those of correct labels, and FLOOR goes between the two. A higher
# FLOOR leaves more enrolled people's utterances V?; a lower one lets more
# people who are not enrolled take someone else's label.
# Re-measure all three on your own rooms.
CEREBELLUM_SPEAKER_UTTERANCE_MIN_S=2
CEREBELLUM_SPEAKER_UTTERANCE_FLOOR=0.65
CEREBELLUM_SPEAKER_UTTERANCE_MARGIN=0.05
# Understander, the FULL chat-completions URL. The client POSTs to exactly this
# string and appends no path.
AMBIENT_UNDERSTAND_URL=http://127.0.0.1:30080/v1/chat/completions
# Served model name at that endpoint. It must match what the endpoint serves
# exactly: on a mismatch the endpoint rejects the request, every judge call
# raises, and every interval settles degraded. No default, so it cannot go
# missing unnoticed.
AMBIENT_UNDERSTAND_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B-FP8
# Judge hard-failure deadline in ms, not an expected latency. A judgment that
# misses it settles its interval as degraded. Must stay below the 10-minute
# silence threshold. Derived for the reference model with the 220-token thinking
# budget, worst completed call: fixed ~0.2 s + 221 reasoning tokens x ~5.9 ms +
# ~300 answer tokens x ~4.7 ms + ~41K uncached prompt tokens x ~0.25 ms
# ~= 13.3 s; 15 s adds margin. Re-derive it for another model or budget.
AMBIENT_UNDERSTAND_TIMEOUT_MS=15000
# Optional bearer credential for the understander, sent as `Authorization: Bearer`.
# Leave it empty for the loopback reference container. Set it to point the judge at
# an OpenAI-compatible API instead; docs/service-contracts.md lists the request
# fields such an endpoint must accept, and the doctrine was measured on the
# reference model only, so a different model is a measurement you run, not a swap.
#AMBIENT_UNDERSTAND_API_KEY=
# Rows of in-connection timeline kept. Not only a memory guard: it is also the
# real bound on the cold-start seed, because the channel hands over the whole
# room context on open and only the last N rows survive here. It is the judge's
# memory length after a restart.
CEREBELLUM_MAX_ROWS=500
# Persistence root for room-local anonymous speaker numbers
# (<dataDir>/speaker-voices/) and for capture orders. Without it every restart
# re-assigns "whoever speaks first is number one" and overwrites the stored
# identity.
CEREBELLUM_DATA_DIR=/opt/ambient/cerebellum/data

# ── Mouth (cloud streaming TTS) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Selected replacement: Alibaba Cloud Model Studio qwen-audio-3.1-tts-flash.
# The endpoint selects the task protocol. Model and voice must match it.
# Replace all three together. See docs/tts-model-selection.md.
TTS_REALTIME_URL=wss://dashscope.aliyuncs.com/api-ws/v1/inference
TTS_MODEL=qwen-audio-3.1-tts-flash
TTS_VOICE=longanlingxin_v3.1
# Cloud credential. User-provided; the process also accepts it from the duoduo
# dotenv file or a workspace config if this is empty.
DASHSCOPE_API_KEY=

# ── Optional ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Expressiveness instruction per speech kind. Omit both to send no instruction.
# The legacy qwen3-tts-flash-realtime model accepts these fields without using
# them. The selected Qwen Audio 3.1 Flash model supports instruction control and
# uses the singular instruction field in its task protocol. Validate delivery
# through generated audio; an echoed field is not evidence of instruction use.
#TTS_INSTRUCTIONS_ACK=
#TTS_INSTRUCTIONS_ANSWER=
# Speech markup ([叹气], <soft>…</soft>) reaches the mouth only when this is on; unset removes it
# before synthesis. Turn it on only for a mouth that performs it, such as drama-3.
#TTS_MARKUP=on
# Debug dumps: the exact judge request body with its response body beside it
# (same stamp; the directory is created 0700 if missing, each file 0600), and,
# into an existing directory, one file per segment of audio.
# Segment audio is unredacted room recording - enable it only for a named experiment, and delete the output
# when that experiment ends.
#CEREBELLUM_DUMP_UNDERSTAND_DIR=
#CEREBELLUM_DUMP_SEGMENTS_DIR=

# ── Read by nothing (kept here only so an old file is not misread) ──────────
# CEREBELLUM_SILENCE_RMS was the energy detector's threshold. That detector was
# deleted when Silero replaced it, and the key is now inert: leaving it in an env
# file changes nothing, and removing it changes nothing.
